<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The kiosk screen: a 1995-flavoured desktop, portrait, read from about 20 cm.

  exit_corner IS STILL HERE, and must stay. It is the only way off this device
  without a factory reset (ten taps, bottom right), and a redesign that quietly
  dropped it would strand the phone. The big clock and its date are gone: the
  time is in the taskbar, bottom right, and the top window is the Google Home
  menu.

  THE DISTANCE CHANGED, AND WITH IT EVERY SIZE IN THIS FILE. The first version
  was set for two metres: a 64sp clock, nothing with a number in it under 20sp.
  Poom reads this the way anyone reads a phone — in the hand, a hand's length
  away — and at 20 cm that scale is a motorway sign. On this device (720x1600
  at 300 dpi, so 384dp wide) a 64sp clock was 4 cm of glass for eight digits,
  and the gold price wrapped its own freshness note onto a second line.
  Everything here is now set for arm's length: 28sp for the hero, 14-15sp for
  numbers you read, 11sp for labels, 8sp for diagnostics.

  TWO FONTS, BOTH SIL OFL, BOTH IN THIS REPOSITORY. Press Start 2P carries the
  digits and Latin; IBM Plex Sans Thai Looped carries Thai and the small print.
  Neither is a Microsoft font and neither is an icon pack — the chrome is still
  layer-list shapes and the icons are still vectors drawn from squares. See
  NOTICE for where the two faces come from and what their licence asks for.
  The mixing inside one line is done in code: see ui/RetroType.kt.

  WHAT IS BIGGEST IS WHAT MATTERS: what Jarvis is doing and what it heard, then
  the numbers, then their labels, then the diagnostics.

  SHARES FOLLOW CONTENT (v0.23). Every window measures its content first and
  then takes a share of what is left over, in proportion to its weight. The
  crypto window already has four coins to show, so an equal share left it the
  loosest-looking box on the screen; it takes 0.25 now. The Google Home
  placeholder has one button and takes 0.7. Weather and gold keep 1 and Jarvis
  2, so what those two gave up goes to the windows with room to use it.

  THE SPARE HEIGHT IS SHARED, NOT HOARDED. Smaller type left about a third of
  the screen over, and the Jarvis window — the only one with a weight — took
  all of it, so the kiosk sat there with a grey box the size of a postcard and
  one line of text in the middle of it. Every window now carries a weight and
  gets a share: one each for the four that hold data, two for Jarvis, which
  still needs the most because it is the one that fills up when somebody talks
  to it. Inside each window the sunken panel carries the same weight again, so
  the share lands in the panel and the content centres in it, rather than
  pooling as dead grey under the last line.

  Those inner panels are wrap_content AND weighted on purpose. A child of a
  wrap_content LinearLayout that asks for 0dp measures to nothing; asking for
  wrap_content and a weight measures to its content first and then grows when
  the parent is re-measured with the share it was given.
-->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@color/retro_desktop">

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:paddingStart="7dp"
        android:paddingEnd="7dp"
        android:paddingBottom="7dp">

        <!-- ======================================================= the card stack
             Every window above Jarvis lives here and is arranged by
             ui/CardBoard: the newest news first, a quiet window folded to its
             title bar, reordered at most once a minute. MainActivity moves the
             views; DESIGN.md, "Cards", has the rules. Jarvis and the taskbar
             are outside this stack and never move. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_stack"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="0dp"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:orientation="vertical">

        <!-- ================================================= google home window -->
        <!-- Where the big clock was. The time lives in the taskbar now, bottom
             right, and only there; this space is the Google Home menu.

             A PLACEHOLDER THIS PHASE. The button is real and tappable and says
             it is not switched on yet — see home/HomeControl, which is the one
             place a real implementation will go in the last phase. Nothing
             behind it talks to Google. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_home"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="0.7"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="5dp">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/home_titlebar"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_titlebar"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:paddingStart="6dp"
                android:paddingEnd="6dp"
                android:paddingTop="2dp"
                android:paddingBottom="2dp">

                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="13dp"
                    android:layout_height="13dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_home"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/window_home" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/home_title"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="5dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:text="@string/window_home"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_title_text"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <!-- "เพิ่งอัปเดต" when this window has news, or its one-line
                     summary when it is folded. Set by MainActivity. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/home_badge"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_badge"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/home_body"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:padding="7dp">

                <!-- A raised 1995 button, the one control on this screen that
                     looks pressable, because it is. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/home_button"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
                    android:clickable="true"
                    android:focusable="true"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:paddingStart="14dp"
                    android:paddingEnd="14dp"
                    android:paddingTop="6dp"
                    android:paddingBottom="6dp"
                    android:text="@string/home_button"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="14sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/home_note"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="5dp"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:text="@string/home_not_connected"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ==================================================== weather window -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_weather"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="5dp">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/weather_titlebar"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_titlebar"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:paddingStart="6dp"
                android:paddingEnd="6dp"
                android:paddingTop="2dp"
                android:paddingBottom="2dp">

                <!-- Swapped for the moon after dark — see MainActivity, which
                     reads the same `is_day` the broker chose the word from, so
                     the picture and the word cannot disagree with each other. -->
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/weather_icon"
                    android:layout_width="13dp"
                    android:layout_height="13dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_sun"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/window_weather" />

                <!-- The place name is appended here at runtime, so this one can
                     grow. One line, cut at the end if it has to be: a title bar
                     that wraps stops looking like a title bar. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/weather_title"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="5dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:text="@string/window_weather"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_title_text"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <!-- "เพิ่งอัปเดต" when this window has news, or its one-line
                     summary when it is folded. Set by MainActivity. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/weather_badge"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_badge"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- The sunken panel is a column now: the reading, and under it one
                 line of sunrise and sunset. The sun line is GONE until both
                 times arrive, so an older broker or a missing value leaves the
                 window exactly as it was rather than showing an empty row. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/weather_panel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:padding="7dp">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/weather_body"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:lineSpacingExtra="1dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="14sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai"
                    android:text="@string/data_loading" />

                <LinearLayout
                    android:id="@+id/sun_row"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
                    android:orientation="horizontal"
                    android:gravity="center_vertical"
                    android:visibility="gone">

                    <ImageView
                        android:layout_width="14dp"
                        android:layout_height="14dp"
                        android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_sunrise"
                        android:contentDescription="@string/sunrise" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/sunrise_text"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="4dp"
                        android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                        android:textSize="12sp"
                        android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                    <ImageView
                        android:layout_width="14dp"
                        android:layout_height="14dp"
                        android:layout_marginStart="16dp"
                        android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_sunset"
                        android:contentDescription="@string/sunset" />

                    <TextView
                        android:id="@+id/sunset_text"
                        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                        android:layout_marginStart="4dp"
                        android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                        android:textSize="12sp"
                        android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
                </LinearLayout>
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ======================================================= gold window -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_gold"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="5dp">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/gold_titlebar"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_titlebar"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:paddingStart="6dp"
                android:paddingEnd="6dp"
                android:paddingTop="2dp"
                android:paddingBottom="2dp">

                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="13dp"
                    android:layout_height="13dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_gold"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/window_gold" />

                <!-- Gains " · เทียบครั้งก่อน" at runtime once there is a
                     percentage beside the prices, and loses it again if there
                     is not. One line, cut at the end if it has to be. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/gold_title"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="5dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:text="@string/window_gold"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_title_text"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <!-- "เพิ่งอัปเดต" when this window has news, or its one-line
                     summary when it is folded. Set by MainActivity. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/gold_badge"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_badge"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- THE COMMODITIES WINDOW (2026-09-23): gold, then fuel, in one
                 sunken panel. Fuel is a step smaller — three lines of the
                 cheapest brands under two gold prices — and GONE until a broker
                 that sends it answers, so an older broker leaves gold alone. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/commodity_panel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:padding="7dp">

                <!-- A TABLE, not paragraphs (2026-09-23): name | price | what
                     follows, each a column, prices right-aligned, so every
                     price sits under the one above it. Each section opens with
                     a one-line header that says what the numbers are — the
                     unit, the basis of the move, "ราคากรุงเทพฯ" and the date —
                     instead of a footnote under them. Rows are built in
                     MainActivity.showCommodities from DashboardState.commodities.
                     DESIGN.md, "การ์ดทองและน้ำมัน". -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/gold_header"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai"
                    android:text="@string/data_loading" />

                <TableLayout
                    android:id="@+id/gold_table"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:shrinkColumns="2"
                    android:stretchColumns="2" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/oil_header"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai"
                    android:visibility="gone" />

                <TableLayout
                    android:id="@+id/oil_table"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:shrinkColumns="2"
                    android:stretchColumns="2"
                    android:visibility="gone" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ===================================================== crypto window -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_crypto"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="0.25"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="5dp">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/crypto_titlebar"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_titlebar"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:paddingStart="6dp"
                android:paddingEnd="6dp"
                android:paddingTop="2dp"
                android:paddingBottom="2dp">

                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="13dp"
                    android:layout_height="13dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_coin"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/window_crypto" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/crypto_title"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="5dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:text="@string/window_crypto"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_title_text"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <!-- "เพิ่งอัปเดต" when this window has news, or its one-line
                     summary when it is folded. Set by MainActivity. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/crypto_badge"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_badge"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- TWO COLUMNS, each coin two lines, dealt two and two: a coin on
                 one line is about 230dp in the pixel face. Not one TextView with
                 spaces between the columns: the pixel font is monospaced and the
                 Thai font beside it is not, so nothing would line up.

                 SIZED TO THE TEXT, NOT TO HALF THE WINDOW. Each column used to
                 be a weighted half, which parked the right-hand pair at the
                 window's midline however short the numbers were and left a
                 gutter you could drive through. Now both wrap their content,
                 sit together in the middle with a fixed gap, and the type scale
                 is untouched. The widest column today is "BTC +0.13%" at about
                 130dp, so two of them and the gap are well inside 350dp. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/crypto_panel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:padding="7dp">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/crypto_body"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:lineSpacingExtra="1dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="15sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai"
                    android:text="@string/data_loading" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/crypto_body_right"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="28dp"
                    android:lineSpacingExtra="1dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="15sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ======================================================= alarms window
             Hidden until there is an alarm. While one rings it is pinned open
             at the top of the stack with a big stop button — the one control
             that must be found in the dark. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_alarms"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_weight="0.5"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="5dp"
            android:visibility="gone">

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/alarms_titlebar"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_titlebar"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:paddingStart="6dp"
                android:paddingEnd="6dp"
                android:paddingTop="2dp"
                android:paddingBottom="2dp">

                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="13dp"
                    android:layout_height="13dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_bell"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/window_alarms" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/alarms_title"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="5dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:ellipsize="end"
                    android:text="@string/window_alarms"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_title_text"
                    android:textSize="11sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <!-- "เพิ่งอัปเดต" when this window has news, or its one-line
                     summary when it is folded. Set by MainActivity. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/alarms_badge"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
                    android:maxLines="1"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_badge"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/alarms_panel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:orientation="vertical"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:padding="7dp">

                <!-- Only while ringing: big, raised, the whole width. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/alarm_stop"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginBottom="6dp"
                    android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
                    android:clickable="true"
                    android:focusable="true"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:minHeight="56dp"
                    android:paddingTop="10dp"
                    android:paddingBottom="10dp"
                    android:text="@string/alarm_stop"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="18sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai"
                    android:visibility="gone" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/alarms_body"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:lineSpacingExtra="1dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="14sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>
        <!-- ======================================================= end of stack -->

        <!-- ===================================================== jarvis window -->
        <!-- FIXED: same place, same size, always (Poom, 2026-09-23). 156dp is
             the height it had on 0.30.3, measured from the A07's screenshot,
             which Poom judged right. The card stack above takes whatever is
             left; when windows fold, THEY give up room, never this one. -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/card_jarvis"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="156dp"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="5dp">

            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_titlebar"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:paddingStart="6dp"
                android:paddingEnd="6dp"
                android:paddingTop="3dp"
                android:paddingBottom="3dp">

                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="15dp"
                    android:layout_height="15dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_jarvis"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/app_name" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/jarvis_state"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="5dp"
                    android:text="@string/jarvis_ready"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_title_text"
                    android:textSize="12sp"
                    android:textStyle="bold"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- SCROLLS (2026-09-23): a 161-character answer ran past the bottom
                 of this window and could not be read. A finger scrolls it, and
                 while the answer is being said it follows the voice on its own
                 (ui/SpeechFollow) until somebody touches it. The scroll bar is
                 always drawn, in the window's own grey, so it is plain that
                 there is more below — DESIGN.md, "Cards".

                 fillViewport so a short line still fills the window and sits
                 centred in it, the way it did before this was a ScrollView.

                 A RestingScrollView, not a plain one: a plain ScrollView made
                 the window as tall as the answer and crushed the windows above
                 it (0.30.0 on the A07). minHeight is the window's resting size
                 — about the one-line invitation it held before — and its
                 weight share is added on top as for every other window. -->
            <com.mammonrn.phoneaikiosk.ui.RestingScrollView
                android:id="@+id/transcript_scroll"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="0dp"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:minHeight="48dp"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:padding="3dp"
                android:fillViewport="true"
                android:scrollbars="vertical"
                android:fadeScrollbars="false"
                android:scrollbarStyle="insideInset"
                android:scrollbarSize="6dp"
                android:scrollbarThumbVertical="@drawable/retro_raised"
                android:scrollbarTrackVertical="@drawable/retro_scroll_track"
                android:overScrollMode="never">

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/transcript"
                    android:layout_width="match_parent"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:padding="5dp"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:lineSpacingExtra="2dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="15sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai"
                    android:text="@string/kiosk_prompt" />
            </com.mammonrn.phoneaikiosk.ui.RestingScrollView>

            <!-- Diagnostics. HIDDEN unless debug mode is switched on over adb
                 (VoiceState.showDiagnostics, TEST_DIAGNOSTICS): the household
                 reads Jarvis's state from the title bar in words, and every
                 line that used to be here is in dumpsys instead. Carries no
                 token and no key — see VoiceState.statusLine. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/voice_status"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:visibility="gone"
                android:layout_marginTop="3dp"
                android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                android:textSize="8sp"
                android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ========================================================== taskbar -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:orientation="horizontal"
            android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:layout_marginTop="7dp"
            android:padding="3dp">

            <!-- THE JARVIS BUTTON, pressable now: the same as saying "Hey
                 Jarvis" — beep, "ฟังอยู่ครับ", then the question. Ignored while
                 a turn is under way (CaptureMachine.canStartByButton), so a
                 press can never start a second turn on top of the first.
                 Bottom LEFT; the exit is bottom RIGHT and untouched. Padding
                 grown to a finger's worth without making the taskbar taller
                 than the clock tray beside it. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/jarvis_button"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_raised"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:contentDescription="@string/jarvis_button_description"
                android:paddingStart="14dp"
                android:paddingEnd="14dp"
                android:paddingTop="6dp"
                android:paddingBottom="6dp"
                android:text="@string/taskbar_button"
                android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                android:textSize="11sp"
                android:textStyle="bold"
                android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

            <!-- THE CONTROL PANEL, opened from here: a raised button with our
                 own panel icon, a thumb wide, beside the Jarvis button — on the
                 LEFT, well away from the exit corner on the right. -->
            <FrameLayout
                android:id="@+id/settings_button"
                android:layout_width="48dp"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:layout_marginStart="4dp"
                android:minHeight="40dp"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_button"
                android:clickable="true"
                android:focusable="true"
                android:contentDescription="@string/settings_open">

                <ImageView
                    android:layout_width="24dp"
                    android:layout_height="24dp"
                    android:layout_gravity="center"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_control_panel"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no" />
            </FrameLayout>

            <!-- owner= lock= awake= token= taps=. INVISIBLE, not gone, unless
                 debug mode is on: it still takes the middle of the taskbar so
                 the clock tray stays pinned right, the way a 1995 taskbar is
                 empty between its button and its tray. Everything it said is in
                 dumpsys as `kiosk :`. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/status"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:visibility="invisible"
                android:layout_marginStart="6dp"
                android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                android:textSize="8sp"
                android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

            <!-- THE ONLY CLOCK ON THE SCREEN, bottom right, 12-hour with AM/PM
                 as Poom asked, in a tray the height of the Jarvis button
                 beside it — one line, like a 1995 system tray, not a second
                 window. Poom found the two-line 11sp version too big for the
                 taskbar. The date stays, before the time, a step dimmer.

                 Sizes: Press Start 2P draws much larger than Plex at the same
                 sp (its digits are 0.875 em tall against Plex's 0.698 cap), so
                 9sp pixel sits level with the 11sp Thai on the button, and
                 still reads at arm's length.

                 Sits under exit_corner, which is transparent and takes the
                 taps; nothing here is clickable, so nothing competes with the
                 way out. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:background="@drawable/retro_sunken"
                android:paddingStart="7dp"
                android:paddingEnd="7dp"
                android:paddingTop="5dp"
                android:paddingBottom="5dp">

                <!-- The phone's own battery: a small pixel battery and the
                     percentage in words. First in the tray because it is the
                     least read; the time stays at the right edge. -->
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/battery_icon"
                    android:layout_width="14dp"
                    android:layout_height="14dp"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_pixel_battery"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/battery_description" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/battery_text"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginStart="2dp"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="7dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/taskbar_date"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginEnd="6dp"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_dim"
                    android:textSize="10sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/plex_thai" />

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/taskbar_clock"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:textColor="@color/retro_text"
                    android:textSize="9sp"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/press_start_2p" />
            </LinearLayout>
        </LinearLayout>
    </LinearLayout>

    <!--
      THE WAY OFF THIS DEVICE. Ten taps in the bottom-right corner.

      Invisible on purpose and last in the file so it sits above everything: a
      Device Owner in lock task mode cannot be left any other way without a
      factory reset. Do not move it, do not shrink it, and do not put anything
      clickable under it.
    -->
    <View
        android:id="@+id/exit_corner"
        android:layout_width="72dp"
        android:layout_height="72dp"
        android:layout_gravity="bottom|end"
        android:background="@android:color/transparent"
        android:contentDescription="@null" />
</FrameLayout>
